{
  "_doc": "yakOS model catalog (K-138). Entries follow the models.dev shape (name, family, modalities, limit, cost) plus yakOS keys: provider (who serves the model, and so receives the request), harnesses (the runtimes whose model flag takes this id), billing (subscription | api | local), effort_levels, effort_in_id, default_enabled. cost (USD per million tokens) exists only on billing=api entries; tokens are the accounting unit for everything else. The aliases key is the semantic alias table (alias -> runtime -> model id) and must stay equal to the aliases key of lib/settings/model-aliases.json, which the bash CLI reads (cli/lib/project-config.sh): TestCatalogAliasesMatchLegacyFile fails on drift. Codex aliases are empty on purpose, as there: an empty value means the harness default and no -m flag, because the codex catalog is per login and plan and gives no documented tiers; map them per operator in ~/.yakos-state/model-registry.yml. The embedded copy cli-go/internal/modelreg/model-catalog.json must equal this file (TestEmbeddedCatalogMatchesLib; refresh with cp).",
  "schema": 1,
